# Type-only `.ts` files

Type-only modules contain **no runtime code**. Only type syntax and ambient declarations.

## Allowed

- `import type { … } from '…'`
- `export type { … }` and `export type Name = …`
- `declare module '…' { … }` and `declare global { … }` (augmentations)
- Type operators: `ReturnType<typeof fn>`, unions, `Pick`, etc. — when `fn` is imported with `import type`

## Not allowed

- `import { … }` (value import)
- `export { … }` (value export)
- `export const` / `let` / `function` / `class` / runtime `enum`
- `Object.freeze`, side-effect `import 'pkg'`

## Pattern

```ts
import type { findInstanceRoot } from '@qctl/shared'

export type InstanceRoot = NonNullable<ReturnType<typeof findInstanceRoot>>

export type SyncResult = {
  synced: number
  skipped: number
}
```

## Module augmentation

```ts
declare module 'yargs' {
  interface Argv {
    // …
  }
}
```

In `.js` (checkJs), `@import` only brings **named types** into JSDoc — it cannot load `declare module` side effects. Keep augmentations in `.ts` files listed in `tsconfig` `include`.
